            <ArticleTitle>Examination and diagnosis of common craniomandibular disorders.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>14-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The disorders of the craniomandibular complex are often a combination of disorders of the temporomandibular joint itself as well as the orofacial and neck muscular. A definitive diagnosis and subsequent treatment plan can only be reached by gaining sufficient information to allow a decision as to which components of the craniomandibular complex, and to what extent, are contributing to the patients problem. A systematic approach to an examination procedure commencing with a simple screening evaluation is discussed, which, when followed, will allow a differential diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
